.TH LSTAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
lstat \- obtain metadata without following the final symbolic link
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/stat.h>
.PP
.BI "int lstat(const char* " path ", struct stat* " buffer ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lstat
stores metadata for the final path component itself, including when it is a
symbolic link. The writable structure has the Linux x86\-64 layout described in
.BR stat (3crunch).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged, or \-1 on failure with positive Linux
.B errno .
.SH NOTES
Include
.B <errno.h>
for error constants. Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stat (3crunch),
.BR readlink (3crunch),
.BR lstat (2)
